    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0`). The audit output confirms the new behaviour end-to-end:\n\n```\nAUDIT - {\"schemaVersion\":2,\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSWV22716E6609E7\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"ownerSegment\":\"STANDARD_METRO\",\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\n## What I changed\n\n**Version-2 identity derivation** \u2014 the `V2` tag is mixed *inside* each identifier only:\n- `OwnerMemberId.base` \u2014 memberId region segment now `region + \"V2\"` \u2192 e.g. `NSWV227\u2026` (one line).\n- `OwnerIdentityKey.of` \u2014 identityKey hashes `\"V2|\" + tel|email|soundex(lastName)` (one line).\n- `OwnerIdentityKey.householdId` \u2014 householdId hashes `\"V2|\" + lastName|postcode` (one line).\n\nBecause the hash inputs / memberId prefix all differ, every identifier changes and no v1 value is reproduced. `OwnerMemberId.region()` is untouched, so `locality` stays the plain code (`NSW`), and `timezone` and `OwnerSegment`'s region are likewise unaffected \u2014 the tag appears only in identifiers.\n\n**Response shape** (`openapi.yml` + `OwnerMapper`):\n- New `OwnerIdentity` schema grouping `memberId`/`householdId`/`identityKey`; those three removed from the top level of `Owner`.\n- Added top-level integer `apiVersion` (constant `2`) and `identity` (a small `default toIdentity(owner)` mapper method builds it).\n\n**Audit event** (`OwnerCreatedEventAdvice`): added `schemaVersion: 2` and `ownerSegment` (recomputed via `OwnerSegment.of(owner)`); the identifier it logs is now the V2 memberId since `customerCode` is V2-derived.\n\n**Two consumers** of the moved DTO getters (`OwnerMembershipCapAdvice`, `OwnerPossibleDuplicateAdvice`) updated to read through `getIdentity()` (one line each).\n\nTo keep structural impact low, changes are single-line edits in small helper classes (low surrounding complexity) plus one new tiny cohesive `toIdentity` unit, rather than growing any existing method or class.",
