    "probe_text": "Here is everything that happens when you `POST /api/owners`, in execution order. The controller/service themselves are trivial (a two-line handler, a one-line `save`); nearly all the behavior is bolted on via 12 `RequestBodyAdvice` classes, 6 AOP aspects around `saveOwner`, 5 `ResponseBodyAdvice` classes, and a servlet filter \u2014 all under `src/main/java/.../rest/advice/`.\n\n## Authorization (first)\n- **`@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`** on `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:99`) \u2014 requires authority `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`. *Only enforced when `petclinic.security.enable=true`.*\n\n## Bean Validation on the request DTO (`OwnerFieldsDto`, enforced by `@Valid @RequestBody`)\nFailures here \u2192 **400** via `ExceptionControllerAdvice.handleMethodArgumentNotValidException`.\n- `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n- `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(...\\.?$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n- `title` \u2014 `@Size(max 3)`\n- `address` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`; `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`\n- `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n- `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$)`, `@Size(1..20)`\n- `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`\n- `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`\n- `registrationDate`, `birthDate` \u2014 `@Valid` ISO dates\n\n## Phase A \u2014 `RequestBodyAdvice` (after JSON parse, before controller)\nAll 12 share `@Order(HIGHEST_PRECEDENCE)`, so **their order relative to each other is not deterministic** (only `beforeBodyRead` before `afterBodyRead` is guaranteed). Each either mutates or validates the DTO:\n\n1. **Idempotency check** (`OwnerIdempotentCreateAdvice`) \u2014 if `Idempotency-Key` header already maps to an owner, short-circuits and replays the original (200, or 404 if gone).\n2. **Address normalization** (`OwnerAddressNormalizationAdvice`) \u2014 trims/collapses whitespace, upper-cases, expands ST\u2192STREET/RD\u2192ROAD/AVE\u2192AVENUE; composes `address` from line1/line2. *(mutation)*\n3. **Email normalization** (`OwnerEmailNormalizationAdvice`) \u2014 lower-case/strip; bad format \u2192 `InvalidEmailException` **400**.\n4. **Telephone normalization** (`OwnerTelephoneNormalizationAdvice`) \u2014 rewrites to E.164 (assumes +61, drops leading 0), checks national length \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` **400**.\n5. **Registration-date defaulting** (`OwnerRegistrationDateAdvice`) \u2014 sets `registrationDate` to the effective business day (missing\u2192today, then rolls weekends/2026 holidays forward). *(mutation)*\n6. **Future-date check** (`OwnerFutureRegistrationDateAdvice`) \u2014 supplied date after today \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` **400**. *(ordering vs. #5 is non-deterministic)*\n7. **Postcode-band check** (`OwnerPostcodeValidationAdvice`) \u2014 for Sydney/Melbourne/Brisbane enforces NSW 2000-2099 / VIC 3000-3099 / QLD 4000-4099 \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` **400**.\n8. **Disposable-email check** (`OwnerDisposableEmailAdvice`) \u2014 rejects mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail \u2192 `DisposableEmailException` **400**.\n9. **Required-fields check** (`OwnerFieldsValidationAdvice`) \u2014 blank firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` **400** (`{\"errors\":[...]}`).\n10. **City capacity** (`OwnerCityCapacityAdvice`) \u2014 \u2265 50 owners in the same city \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` **409**. *(full-table scan)*\n11. **Daily creation limit** (`OwnerDailyCreationLimitAdvice`) \u2014 \u2265 100 owners for the effective business day \u2192 `DailyLimitReachedException` **429**. *(scan)*\n12. **Unique identity** (`OwnerUniqueIdentityAdvice`) \u2014 duplicate `OwnerIdentityKey` among non-deleted owners \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` **409**. *(scan)*\n\n## Phase B \u2014 DTO\u2192entity mapping\n`OwnerMapper.toOwner` copies fields (`id`/`pets` ignored); `deleted` defaults to `FALSE`.\n\n## Phase C \u2014 AOP `@Before` aspects around `saveOwner` (mutate, then persisted; each guarded by `owner.isNew() && field==null`)\n- **Household size** (`OwnerHouseholdSizeAdvice`) \u2014 sets `householdSize` = count sharing the household id + 1. *(scan)*\n- **Namesake count** (`OwnerNamesakeCountAdvice`) \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = count of same first+last name. *(scan)*\n- **Customer code** (`OwnerCustomerCodeAdvice`) \u2014 sets `customerCode` (region + \"V2\" + FY + SHA-256 prefix + Luhn digit), de-duplicated with `-2`, `-3`\u2026 suffixes on collision.\n\n*(order among these three is not guaranteed)*\n\n## Phase D \u2014 persistence\n- **`ownerRepository.save(owner)`** inside `@Transactional ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner` \u2014 persists the single `Owner` row (id DB-generated). No lifecycle callbacks (`@PrePersist`/`@PreUpdate`) exist. No other entity is created or mutated.\n\n## Phase C\u2032 \u2014 AOP `@Around` side-effects (after successful save, only when new)\nAll three are just SLF4J log lines (no real email/bus):\n- **Audit log** (`OwnerAuditCreationAdvice`) \u2014 `AUDIT` \"owner created \u2026\".\n- **Created event** (`OwnerCreatedEventAdvice`) \u2014 `AUDIT` structured JSON `OWNER_CREATED` event.\n- **Welcome notification** (`OwnerWelcomeNotificationAdvice`) \u2014 `NOTIFY` welcome enqueue.\n\n## Phase E/F \u2014 response mapping + `ResponseBodyAdvice` (after save, before serialization)\n`OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto` computes read-only derived fields (displayName, memberId, membershipLevel, segment, etc. \u2014 no side effects). Then 5 advices mutate the outgoing DTO (several re-scan all owners): possible-duplicate flag, bulk-signup warning, capacity warning, risk flag, and membership-level cap; the idempotency advice records `key \u2192 owner id`.\n\n## Phase G \u2014 response filter\n- **`ProblemJsonRejectionFilter`** \u2014 rewrites 400/409/429 bodies into RFC-7807 `application/problem+json`.\n\n---\n\n**Caveats the code makes clear:** the 12 request-body advices share the same order, so validations like registration-date defaulting vs. the future-date check can run in either order; the capacity/limit/unique checks in Phase A rely on live scans / in-memory state and are **not** re-checked atomically at save time; and `findAllOwners()` is scanned ~7\u00d7 per create."
